    "note": "ClientHello, HTTP/2 frames and header sets are those captured for firefox-144-macos; wreq-util declares firefox 147 to use the same TLS and HTTP/2 configuration (ff147: tls_options!('4', 'CIPHER_LIST_1', 'CURVES_2', 'KEY_SHARES_2'), http2_options!(1)). The User-Agent is wreq-util's; accept-language is wreq-util's. Nothing was seen on the wire for this version here. wreq-util declares Firefox 136 to 151 equal to 135; the Firefox 155 and 156 captured here differ (15 ciphers, no FFDHE groups), so where the change happened is unknown."
